For Python symbol-aware navigation (definitions, references, implementations,
and call hierarchy), prefer the ty LSP over `grep`/`rg` when the LSP is
available and can answer the question. Use text search for literals, configs,
non-Python files, broad discovery, or when the LSP cannot provide the result.

Exclude `.pixi/` from filesystem and text searches by default, including with
`find`, `rg`, `grep`, and similar tools. Search it when intentionally inspecting
the Pixi environment or its installed packages, such as locating third-party
package source, examining site-packages, or debugging environment setup.

Never run a blanket recursive text or filename search over the home directory
or filesystem root, such as `rg`, `grep`, or `find` rooted at `/`, `~`, or
`$HOME`, without first requesting explicit approval. Narrow searches to known
project or task-relevant subdirectories. Read a known path directly instead of
searching to locate it.

## Codex workflow routing

Resolve each workflow name in the shared instructions as the Codex skill with
the same name, invoked as `$<name>`.

<!-- include: common.md -->

## Shell

- Set shell tool calls to `login: false` unless the task explicitly tests login
  or profile startup. Routine commands must not source interactive or login
  shell configuration.
- For a requested deletion of a Git-tracked path, first inspect its exact
  status and diff for uncommitted content, then use `git rm -- <path>`. Git
  history preserves committed content; do not route tracked files through
  `/mnt/main0/.vast_trash`.
- For an untracked or non-versioned path, first confirm its exact scope and
  move it into `/mnt/main0/.vast_trash` under a collision-free name. If that
  destination rejects the move, delete the same exact target normally; do not
  broaden or recompute the target between attempts. Treat the trash as
  temporary, not archival; content that must be retained needs an explicit
  durable destination.
- Test bootstrap and PATH behavior with `env -i`; a new interactive shell
  inherits exported state and is not a clean environment.
- For a temporary mutation or bisect probe, assert that the change applied,
  restore it on every exit path, and verify the final Git status. Do not start
  when unrelated work cannot be preserved.
